@tradition sunday-story
// The Sunday story (FX14, 0.92.5 item 16; SW1's pitch): a bedtime story for grown-ups. After his last round of the decks
// on Sunday, Chief Holt reads one chapter of a long adventure book in the junior common room, doing the voices, badly.
// Behind WEEKEND_ON. The chapters themselves are a writing job (SW1): a few to start.
k: 464
title: The Sunday story
when: weekly sunday
at: 22:15-22:55
min: 25
jitter: 5
where: 4 pool common-room
hold: 1
who: holt always, night-owl 50%, juniors 45%, common-room 40%, everyone 8%
anim: holt read, everyone none
host: holt
from: holt

== mail
- Chapter nine tomorrow at 22:15. The common room. Be on time. I don't recap.

== ask
- The Sunday story later? Holt's doing the pirate voice again.   #funny
- Story time tonight in the common room. Don't tell anyone you're coming for the voices.

== here
- Shh. He's getting to the storm.
- That's not what a parrot sounds like. Don't tell him.   #funny

== thanks
- You settle on a beanbag while Chief Holt reads the next chapter, doing all the voices, badly. Nobody admits they love it.

== chatter
- Did you hear what happened in the story last night? I'll tell you at breakfast.
